Font Awesome standalone Rust V2

Derived from https://github.com/almatkai/fontawesome at
39549ced40cbe73492213e731064404dde84d165 (MIT declaration, author almatkai),
and Raycast extensions/fontawesome at
6734d85992290066fd31a7f5bee3cca3d3545a1a (author dutzi and manifest contributors).
Original code, command PNG and 17 style assets are preserved in fixtures/source
and resources. Raycast repository MIT license (Copyright 2021 Raycast) is
included verbatim as LICENSE and licenses/raycast-upstream/LICENSE.
The source repository's LICENSE contains literal backslash-n sequences;
licenses/fontawesome-source/LICENSE preserves those original bytes.

Port changes: independent Rust process, HTTPS/OAuth/GraphQL client, bounded
credential/profile/settings-scoped volatile caches, private remembered selection
storage, strict host ACK and lifecycle fencing, inert SVG previews, tests and
private packaging. No Raycast JavaScript runtime is shipped.

Independent tezbar-extension-sdk 0.1.1 is pinned to
https://github.com/almatkai/tezbar-extension-sdk-rust.git at
e955911f0bf5b558f9d3eb5183df0adc95c22af2, Apache-2.0. Its original LICENSE and
NOTICE are included under licenses/tezbar-extension-sdk-0.1.1/.

Locked runtime and QA crate metadata and original available license texts are
recorded in resources/provenance/DEPENDENCIES.json and licenses/. A missing text is explicitly marked
there, never replaced with an invented grant. Font Awesome service access and
Pro icon rights remain governed by the user's Font Awesome account and terms;
this port grants no additional rights to service-returned icons. No live icon
catalog or Pro icon content has been bundled. The pinned upstream repository
license is the available provenance evidence for the original command assets;
no separate asset-specific grant has been invented.
